<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       GLITTERHEARTS STAY OUT OF THE GENERAL REWARD POOLS

       An earlier version of this file added glitterhearts to Odyssey's
       Reward_GravshipUpgrade. That has been removed, for two reasons.

       1. IT LEAKED BACK ONTO EARTH. Reward_GravshipUpgrade is not used only
          by the two orbital quests. It is also the <contents> of
          AncientSealedContainer_GravshipUpgrade, which spawns in
          LayoutRooms_AncientRuins.xml - SURFACE ancient ruins. So the patch
          quietly undid what Ascension_NoEarthHearts had just done.

       2. IT WAS NOT ADDITIVE IN PRACTICE. Reward_GravshipUpgrade has four
          vanilla options totalling weight 3.75 (FuelOptimizer 1,
          GravshipShieldGenerator 1, PilotSubpersonaCore 1, Gravcore 0.75).
          Adding weights 3+5+2 made glitterhearts 73% of the maker and pushed
          Gravcore from 20% down to 5.5%. Gravcore is core Odyssey gravship
          progression. Structurally additive, materially a 3.6x cut.

       Hearts now come from exactly two places, both of which require going
       up and both of which are Glitterite-owned:

         - Glitterite orbital settlements, via settlementLootMaker on their
           FactionDef. 3~5 per base, guaranteed.
         - Glittership chunks on orbital platforms and wrecks, via
           Archinity_GlittershipDebris. 3 hearts each, 20000 work to break.

       Odyssey's own reward tables are left exactly as shipped.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <!-- Glitterite raiders still carry them. This is the one surface-side
       source, and it is deliberate: it requires beating an Ultra-tech raid
       that cannot fire before day 400 and 3000 threat points. You took it
       off their bodies, which is the same story as taking it off their base. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="Ushanka.GlittertechExpansion">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingSetMakerDef[defName="Archinity_GlitteritesRaidLootMaker"]/root/fixedParams/filter/thingDefs</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>USH_Glitterheart</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- USH_Glitterheart ships with thingSetMakerTags RewardStandardLowFreq,
       which enrols it in Reward_ItemsStandard - the generic quest reward
       maker used by SURFACE quests. Removing the tag closes the last route
       by which a heart could arrive without leaving the planet.

       Removing the whole node rather than one <li>: RewardStandardLowFreq is
       the only tag on the def, and an empty <thingSetMakerTags> list is not
       the same as absent to ThingSetMakerUtility. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove" MayRequire="Ushanka.GlittertechExpansion">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="USH_Glitterheart"]/thingSetMakerTags</xpath>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
